Boot Procedure & Break root password
====================================
1. Step-by-step Linux Boot / Reboot Flow
🔁 What happens when reboot command is given ?
Step 1: User runs
reboot
Step 2: systemd receives signal
(systemctl reboot)
Step 3: Stop all services
systemctl stops running services gracefully
Step 4: Unmount filesystems
umount all mounted partitions
Step 5: Sync data to disk
sync → flush memory buffers
Step 6: Kill remaining processes
Step 7: Kernel triggers reboot


2. Full Boot Flow (VERY IMPORTANT INTERVIEW)
Step 1: BIOS / UEFI
✔ Hardware check (POST)
✔ Looks for bootable device

Step 2: Bootloader (GRUB2)
✔ Loads kernel and initramfs
✔ Displays boot menu

Step 3: Kernel loads
✔ Kernel initializes hardware
✔ Mounts root filesystem (temporary via initramfs)

Step 4: initramfs
✔ Temporary root filesystem
✔ Loads drivers required to mount real root

Step 5: Switch to real root filesystem
✔ Mount actual / (root)

Step 6: systemd (PID 1)
✔ Starts system services
✔ Reads target

Step 7: Target reached
✔ multi-user.target OR graphical.target


3. Root Password Reset (Break Root Password)
✅ Works for RHEL 7 / 8 / 9 (slight difference)

🔴 Method 1: Using GRUB (Most important)

Step-by-step (common logic for RHEL 7/8/9)

Step 1: Reboot system

Step 2: At GRUB menu
Press e (edit mode)

Step 3: Find kernel line
Look for line starting with:
linux or linux16 or linuxefi

Step 4: Modify line
👉 Remove:
rhgb quiet
👉 Add at end:
For RHEL 7:
rd.break
For RHEL 8/9:
rd.break

Step 5: Boot
Press:
Ctrl + X


4. Enter emergency shell
Step 1: System drops to initramfs shell

Step 2: Remount root filesystem as read-write
mount -o remount,rw /sysroot

Step 3: Change root
chroot /sysroot


5. Reset root password
passwd
👉 Enter new password


6. Fix SELinux context (VERY IMPORTANT)
For RHEL 8/9:
touch /.autorelabel
👉 Required for SELinux systems


7. Exit and reboot
Step 1: Exit chroot
exit
Step 2: Exit again
exit
Step 3: System reboots


8. First boot after reset
Step 1: SELinux relabel starts
✔ May take time
Step 2: Login with new password


9. RHEL 7 vs 8/9 difference (INTERVIEW)
RHEL 7:
✔ Sometimes no SELinux relabel needed
RHEL 8/9:
✔ Must run
touch /.autorelabel


10. Alternative method (less used)
Add to kernel line:
init=/bin/bash

Steps
Step 1: Edit grub → add init=/bin/bash
Step 2: Boot
Step 3: Mount root RW
mount -o remount,rw /
Step 4: Change password
passwd
Step 5: Exec init
exec /sbin/init


11. Real production scenario (password reset not working)

Problem 1: System read-only
Fix:
mount -o remount,rw /sysroot

Problem 2: SELinux blocking login
Fix:
touch /.autorelabel

Problem 3: Keyboard issue / wrong input
✔ Check keyboard layout


12. Security concept (IMPORTANT)
👉 Why this works ?
Step 1: Physical access to system
Step 2: GRUB allows kernel edit
Step 3: Bypass authentication

How to prevent ?
Step 1: Set GRUB password
grub2-setpassword


13. Important interview questions

Why chroot is used ?
✔ To switch into real root filesystem


What is rd.break ?
✔ Break boot process before mounting root


Why remount rw required ?
✔ Root partition mounted as read-only


What happens if you skip autorelabel ?
✔ Login may fail due to SELinux context mismatch


14. Quick revision
reboot → stop services → unmount → restart
GRUB → kernel edit → rd.break
mount → chroot → passwd
SELinux → autorelabel



